{
  "description": "The merge back of an edited stripped rendition onto its document of record (SOM §11.10; the reading view's part *Stripped renditions and the merge back*). Maintained by hand. valueCases: `original` stripped with the switches (`drop`, `unmark`, `appendix`, `appendixReferences`), each `[find, replace]` of `edits` applied to the stripped text (each find occurs once), and `expect` the toJson of mergeStrippedValue(original, stripped, edited, pieces): `text` (null on a conflict), `restored` (pieces put back), `placed` (`at` in the merged text, `removed`) and `conflicts` (`code`, `removed`). documentCases: `state` stripped over the corpus model and schema with the switches and `source` into a readable rendition, the `edits` applied to it, and SpecStripMerge.merge of that onto `current` (else `state`) with `currentRevision`, `options` (switches given beside the header), `base` (given by hand) and `commits` (what the header's commit loads); `expect` is `exitCode`, `stale`, the merged `document` (null when nothing may be written) and the `report` lines, or `error` for a usage error.",
